    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <h3><a name="Motivation"></a>Motivation</h3>

<p><a href="https://t.me/c/2126426325/30490" title="smart-link" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://t.me/c/2126426325/30490</a> </p>

<p>The YDB team would like to see more links displayed in the UI on cluster and database pages.<br/>
Currently, only a very limited number of links can be configured. For example, it’s not possible to set up multiple monitoring links. Each customization requires a manual change in the UI, which is inconvenient and time-consuming.</p>

<p>Team wants to be able to add new links more quickly — for example, multiple links to dashboards or graphs, if needed.</p>

<p>Vlad Kuznecov mentioned these dashboards for database page:<br/>
<a href="https://grafana.nebius.dev/goto/xiSvjIaHg?orgId=1" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://grafana.nebius.dev/goto/xiSvjIaHg?orgId=1</a><br/>
<a href="https://grafana.nebius.dev/goto/hv5djS-NR?orgId=1" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://grafana.nebius.dev/goto/hv5djS-NR?orgId=1</a><br/>
<a href="https://grafana.nebius.dev/goto/YrYOjI-Hg?orgId=1" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://grafana.nebius.dev/goto/YrYOjI-Hg?orgId=1</a></p>

<h2><a name="Scenarios"></a>Scenarios</h2>

<p><b>View cluster dashboards and logs from cluster page</b></p>

<p><b>Actor:</b> YDB UI user<br/>
<b>Goal:</b> Access cluster logs and dashboards using UI<br/>
<b>Steps:</b></p>
<ol>
	<li>The user opens the YDB UI at <tt>ydb.nebius.dev</tt> and navigates to a specific cluster.</li>
	<li>The UI loads cluster information from <tt>Meta</tt>, including available link configuration.</li>
	<li>If tag-based links are configured, the UI requests dashboards from Grafana by tag.</li>
	<li>The UI appends dynamically loaded dashboard links below the existing links.</li>
	<li>The UI displays a vertical list of links in the <tt>Overview -&gt; Details</tt> section (see picture below).</li>
	<li>The user clicks a link.</li>
	<li>A new tab opens in Grafana with auto-filled parameters (<tt>ds</tt>, <tt>workspace</tt>).<br/>
<b>Outcome:</b> The user opens the relevant Grafana dashboard with essential parameters applied and can see all relevant dashboards for the cluster.<br/>
<b>Fallback:</b> If Grafana or dynamic data is unavailable (timeout), only static links are shown and the UI remains fully functional.<br/>
<span class="image-wrap" style=""><img src="/rest/api/3/attachment/content/847345" alt="photo_2025-11-06_10-50-34.jpg" width="430" style="border: 0px solid black" /></span><br/>
<span class="image-wrap" style=""><img src="/rest/api/3/attachment/content/836002" alt="Screenshot 2025-10-16 at 15.29.59.png" width="314" style="border: 0px solid black" /></span></li>
</ol>


<p><b>View database dashboards and logs from cluster page</b></p>

<p><b>Actor:</b> YDB UI user<br/>
<b>Goal:</b> Access database-specific dashboards and logs using the UI<br/>
<b>Steps:</b></p>
<ol>
	<li>The user opens the YDB UI at <tt>ydb.nebius.dev</tt> and navigates to a specific cluster to the <tt>Databases</tt> section.</li>
	<li>The UI loads database information from <tt>Meta</tt>, including available link configuration.</li>
	<li>If tag-based links are configured, the UI requests dashboards from Grafana by tag.</li>
	<li>The UI appends dynamically loaded dashboard links below the existing links.</li>
	<li>When the user hovers over the <b>info <img class="emoticon" src="/images/icons/emoticons/information.png" height="16" width="16" align="absmiddle" alt="" border="0"/></b> icon for a database, the UI shows a vertical list of links in a tooltip.</li>
	<li>The user clicks a link.</li>
	<li>A new tab opens in Grafana with auto-filled parameters (<tt>ds</tt>, <tt>workspace</tt>, <tt>database</tt>).<br/>
<b>Outcome:</b> The user opens the relevant Grafana dashboard with essential parameters applied and can see all relevant dashboards for the database.<br/>
<b>Fallback:</b> If Grafana or dynamic data is unavailable (timeout), only static links are shown and the UI remains fully functional.<br/>
<span class="image-wrap" style=""><img src="/rest/api/3/attachment/content/836003" alt="Screenshot 2025-10-16 at 15.36.18.png" width="564" style="border: 0px solid black" /></span></li>
</ol>


<p><b>View database dashboards and logs from database page</b></p>

<p><b>Actor:</b> YDB UI user<br/>
<b>Goal:</b> Open database-specific dashboards and logs directly from the database page<br/>
<b>Steps:</b></p>
<ol>
	<li>The user opens the YDB UI at <tt>ydb.nebius.dev</tt> and navigates to a specific database.</li>
	<li>The UI loads database information from <tt>Meta</tt>, including available link configuration.</li>
	<li>If tag-based links are configured, the UI requests dashboards from Grafana by tag.</li>
	<li>The UI appends dynamically loaded dashboard links below the existing links.</li>
	<li>The UI displays several link icons in a row (see pictures below), each with a tooltip describing its target dashboard or logs page.</li>
	<li>The user clicks an icon.</li>
	<li>A new tab opens in Grafana with auto-filled parameters (<tt>ds</tt>, <tt>workspace</tt>, <tt>database</tt>).<br/>
<b>Outcome:</b> The user opens the relevant Grafana dashboard with essential parameters applied and can see all relevant dashboards for the database.<br/>
<b>Fallback:</b> If Grafana or dynamic data is unavailable (timeout), only static icons are shown and the UI remains fully functional.<br/>
<span class="image-wrap" style=""><img src="/rest/api/3/attachment/content/847341" alt="Screenshot 2025-11-06 at 10.53.20.png" width="293" style="border: 0px solid black" /></span><br/>
<span class="image-wrap" style=""><img src="/rest/api/3/attachment/content/836031" alt="Screenshot 2025-10-16 at 15.46.19.png" width="554" style="border: 0px solid black" /></span></li>
</ol>


<h3><a name="Possiblesolution"></a>Possible solution</h3>

<p>In the UI, there are links to dashboards for each database and cluster. Currently, the UI gets these links from Meta database, but I’d like to change that so the management of dashboard lists happens on the Grafana side. On the Grafana side, a list of dashboards will be configured for each tag, and Meta will know the tags that the UI can use to load the corresponding links.</p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

    <br/>

    <table cellpadding="2" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center">
    <tr>
        <td bgcolor="#bbbbbb" width="1%" nowrap align="center">
