    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="grid" style="margin: 0;">
                <tr id="comment-header-6513240"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Комментарий по  
                                                    
                
        
            <a class="user-hover" rel="712020:8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f"
                id="word_commented_712020:8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f"
                href="https://nebius.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f">
                    Andrei Rykov
                </a>

                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">09/мая/25</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-6513240"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p>As far as I can see, and the frontend team confirms this, it's currently not possible to define links dynamically.<br/>
In the latest version of the UI, for a cluster you can define:<br/>
<tt>"link_cores": "Coredumps",</tt><br/>
<tt>"link_logging": "Logging",</tt><br/>
<tt>"link_slo-logs": "SLO Logs"</tt><br/>
For a database:<br/>
<tt>"field_monitoring-link": "Monitoring",</tt><br/>
<tt>"field_logs-link": "Logs"</tt></p>

<p>After the holidays, I’ll discuss the required changes.</p>
        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-6524581"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Комментарий по  
                                                    
                
        
            <a class="user-hover" rel="712020:8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f"
                id="word_commented_712020:8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f"
                href="https://nebius.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f">
                    Andrei Rykov
                </a>

                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">15/мая/25</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-6524581"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p>It seems that for database info page, we could use list of links from <a href="https://docs.nebius.dev/en/ydb/quickstart#monitoring" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">ydb docs</a><br/>
<a href="https://grafana.nebius.dev/d/ydb_dbstatus/db-status?orgId=1&amp;refresh=30s&amp;from=now-5m&amp;to=now&amp;timezone=browser&amp;var-ds=b0269287-b776-4e5e-b980-7a731fe272e8&amp;var-workspace=ydb-global&amp;var-database=%2Ftesting-global%2Fbilling" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">DB status</a><br/>
<a href="https://grafana.nebius.dev/d/dedicated-topic-consumer/dedicated-topic-consumer?orgId=1&amp;from=now-7d&amp;to=now&amp;timezone=browser&amp;var-ds=fc872d93-d988-491c-83cd-19249cb962b0&amp;var-workspace=ydb-common&amp;var-bucket=datastreams_serverless&amp;var-database=%2Feu-north1-common%2Frepo-reflog&amp;var-topic=$__all&amp;var-consumer=$__all" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Dedicated Topic Consumer</a><br/>
<a href="https://grafana.nebius.dev/d/b3da8a06-387a-4af6-b8f6-055448f31cb2/user-dashboard-dedicated?orgId=1&amp;from=now-6h&amp;to=now&amp;timezone=browser&amp;var-ds=fc872d93-d988-491c-83cd-19249cb962b0&amp;var-workspace=ydb-common&amp;var-database=%2Feu-north1-common%2Ftemporal" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">User Dashboard</a><br/>
+ logs</p>

<p>Vlad Kuznecov mentioned these dashboards:<br/>
