        <tr id="comment-body-6622756"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <h1><a name="Generatingmonitoringlinks"></a>Generating monitoring links</h1>

<p>The UI receives a response from the meta <tt>/db_clusters</tt>, which includes a new field called <tt>Links</tt><b>.</b><br/>
This field contains a JSON object with link templates, UI could arrange the link from the teplate, display link name, and optionally an icon.</p>

<p>If the <tt>Links</tt> field is not set or empty, links are derived from the <tt>solomon</tt> and <tt>logging_link</tt> fields as before.</p>

<h1><a name="LinkJSONformat"></a>Link JSON format</h1>

<p>The <tt>Links</tt> field in the response contains two arrays:</p>

<ul>
	<li><tt>links</tt> - a list of reusable link definitions</li>
	<li><tt>placements</tt> — rules for assigning links to specific entities and UI scopes</li>
</ul>


<p>Each link in the <tt>links</tt> array includes:</p>

<ul>
	<li><tt>id</tt> - a unique identifier used for reference in placements</li>
	<li><tt>title</tt> - the name shown in the UI</li>
	<li><tt>template</tt> - a URL template with optional placeholder ({{
{dbName}}})<br/>
* <tt>icon</tt> - the icon name referencing an SVG asset<br/>
<br/>
Each entry in the <tt>placements</tt> array defines how links should appear:<br/>
<br/>
* <tt>entity</tt> - the object type the links apply to (<tt>cluster</tt>, <tt>dedicated</tt>, or <tt>serverless</tt>)<br/>
* <tt>scope</tt> - the UI context where the links are shown (<tt>dashboard</tt>, <tt>info</tt>, or <tt>default</tt>)<br/>
* <tt>links</tt> - an array of link <tt>id}}s from the {{links</tt> section<br/>
<br/>
Placements with <tt>scope = "default"</tt> are applied automatically unless overridden by a more specific scope for the same <tt>entity</tt>.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Example:</b><br/>

<div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"><div class="preformattedContent panelContent">
<pre></pre>
</div></div>{<br/>
  "links": [<br/>
    {<br/>
      "id": "db_logs_general",<br/>
      "title": "Logs",<br/>
      "template": "https://logs.example.com/view?db={dbName}
<p>",<br/>
      "icon": "logs"<br/>
    },<br/>
    </p>
{
      "id": "cluster_monitoring",
      "title": "Monitoring",
      "template": "https://grafana.example.com/d/cluster-dashboard",
      "icon": "monitoring"
    }
<p>,<br/>
    </p>
{
      "id": "coredumps",
      "title": "Coredumps",
      "template": "https://core.example.com/view",
      "icon": "coredump"
    }
<p>,<br/>
    {<br/>
      "id": "dedicated_mon",<br/>
      "title": "Monitoring",<br/>
      "template": "https://grafana.example.com/d/dedicated-dashboard?var-db=</p>
{dbName}",<br/>
      "icon": "monitoring"<br/>
    },<br/>
  ],<br/>
  "placements": [<br/>
    {
      "entity": "cluster",
      "scope": "dashboard",
      "links": ["cluster_monitoring"]
    },<br/>
    {
      "entity": "cluster",
      "scope": "info",
      "links": ["coredumps"]
    },<br/>
    {
      "entity": "dedicated",
      "scope": "dashboard",
      "links": ["db_logs_general", "dedicated_mon"]
    },<br/>
    {
      "entity": "dedicated",
      "scope": "default",
      "links": ["db_logs_general"]
    },<br/>
    {
      "entity": "serverless",
      "scope": "info",
      "links": ["db_logs_general"]
    }<br/>
  ]<br/>
}<div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"><div class="preformattedContent panelContent">
<pre></pre>
</div></div><br/>
<br/>
h1. Link creation<br/>
<br/>
When generating links in the UI:<br/>
<br/>
* For <b>clusters</b>, placements are selected where <tt>entity = "cluster"</tt> and <tt>scope</tt> matches the current UI context.<br/>
* For <b>databases</b>, the <tt>entity</tt> is derived from the database type (<tt>dedicated</tt> or <tt>serverless</tt>).<br/>
<br/>
If a placement with the required <tt>scope</tt> exists, it is used. Otherwise, a placement with <tt>scope = "default"</tt> is applied for that entity.<br/>
<br/>
If both are present, links from the specific scope <b>override or extend</b> the default set. Duplicate IDs are allowed and handled according to UI logic.<br/>
<br/>
In all templates, the {{{dbName}
<p>}} placeholder is replaced with the actual database name.</p></li>
</ul>


<h1><a name="Theiconcanbesettooneofthepredefinedtypes%3A"></a>The icon can be set to one of the predefined types:</h1>

<ul>
	<li><tt>logs</tt> - <a href="https://gravity-ui.com/icons?icon=FileText" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://gravity-ui.com/icons?icon=FileText</a></li>
	<li><tt>monitoring</tt> - <a href="https://gravity-ui.com/icons?icon=ChartLine" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://gravity-ui.com/icons?icon=ChartLine</a></li>
	<li><tt>coredump</tt> - <a href="https://gravity-ui.com/icons?icon=Bug" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://gravity-ui.com/icons?icon=Bug</a></li>
	<li><tt>documentaion</tt>- <a href="https://gravity-ui.com/icons?icon=BookOpen" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://gravity-ui.com/icons?icon=BookOpen</a></li>
	<li><tt>link</tt> (used as default if not specified) - <a href="https://gravity-ui.com/icons?icon=Link" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://gravity-ui.com/icons?icon=Link</a></li>
</ul>


<h1><a name="Expectedresult"></a>Expected result</h1>

<p>There are several places in the UI where links are displayed. </p>

<ul>
	<li><tt><span class="error">&#91;cluster&#93;</span><span class="error">&#91;dashboard&#93;</span></tt> On the clusters list page, each link can be shown with its name.</li>
	<li><tt><span class="error">&#91;cluster&#93;</span><span class="error">&#91;info&#93;</span></tt> On the cluster page, each link can be shown with its name.</li>
	<li><tt><span class="error">&#91;dedicated/serverless&#93;</span><span class="error">&#91;dashboard&#93;</span></tt> On the database list page, each link can be shown with its name.</li>
	<li><tt><span class="error">&#91;dedicated/serverless&#93;</span><span class="error">&#91;info&#93;</span></tt> On the database page, at this stage, only the link icons can be displayed, with their names shown in a tooltip.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>cluster list page</b></p>

<p><span class="image-wrap" style=""><img src="/rest/api/3/attachment/content/779857" alt="image-20250703-194232.png" height="484" width="1336" style="border: 0px solid black" /></span></p>

<p><b>cluster page</b></p>

<p><span class="image-wrap" style=""><img src="/rest/api/3/attachment/content/778773" alt="image-20250702-135842.png" height="770" width="831" style="border: 0px solid black" /></span></p>


<p><b>database page</b></p>

<p><span class="image-wrap" style=""><img src="/rest/api/3/attachment/content/778772" alt="image-20250702-140129.png" height="526" width="865" style="border: 0px solid black" /></span></p>


<h1><a name="IntegrationwithUI"></a>Integration with UI</h1>

<p>The table values in the META database need to be updated, and the Nebius UI needs to be updated — these actions can be done in any order.</p>

<h1><a name="Affectedcomponents"></a>Affected components</h1>

<p>We need a change in embedded-ui (already done) and a change in Nebius UI to support parsing the link JSON.<br/>
No changes are needed in YDB.</p>
        </td></tr>
