                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-6936117"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p><a href="https://nebius.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f" class="user-hover" rel="712020:8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f" data-account-id="712020:8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f" accountid="712020:8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f" rel="noreferrer">Andrei Rykov</a> Have read it more carefully, and found that the pictures are ‘as is’, while in the text above there are descriptions of what is to be changed. Then there are comments.</p>

<blockquote><p>in <tt>Overview</tt> - <tt>Details</tt> the user should see a vertical list of links (instead of the Monitoring link shown in the screenshot).</p></blockquote>

<ol>
	<li>We discussed that the new functionality will add options, but not replace them. Logs/Traces/Monitoring are the options which currently exist.</li>
	<li>Vertical list of links – not specified what is in this list. If you mean it’s the list of relevant Dashboards from Grafana, then I would suggest not to do it this way, for two reasons:
	<ol>
		<li>It will consume screen space, the block ‘Storage groups’ may become totally invisible without scrolling</li>
		<li>Looking up in Grafana when rendering the Overview-Details page may result in delays or even failure to display it if something with Grafana integration is not working properly</li>
	</ol>
	</li>
	<li>There’s no mention that the links do not just to dashboards, but have the preinitialised values for parameters ‘data source’ and ‘cluster’ (or which ones?), while it’s the main value brought in by our integration.</li>
</ol>


<blockquote><p>in <tt>Databases</tt> section, the user need to see a vertical list of links in the tooltip (instead of the Monitoring link shown in the screenshot)</p></blockquote>

<ol>
	<li>The same like for the previous – we are adding functionality, not replacing. How the existing links + new functionality will look/work?</li>
	<li>It makes sense to write that when user clicks on the ‘<img class="emoticon" src="/images/icons/emoticons/information.png" height="16" width="16" align="absmiddle" alt="" border="0"/>’ button, a request to Grafana is being made to get a list of relevant Dashboards. Then, the links show are enriched with the values for the ‘database’ field, so that the user goes not just to the dashboard, but also has its ‘datasource’, ‘cluster’ and ‘database’ parameter values preinitialised.</li>
</ol>


<blockquote><p>On the database page, the user needs to see several link icons in line that duplicate the links from the second item (instead of the Monitoring icon shown in the screenshot). When you click on icon, a new window will open with either the dashboard or the logs in Grafana.</p></blockquote>

<ol>
	<li>The same like for the previous 2 citations above.</li>
	<li>That’s not clear for me how do the ‘several link icons’ look like. And again, it you’re going to build them while rendering the page, you’ll have the problem with delays or failures to display the whole page if Grafana integration is not working.</li>
</ol>

        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-7016400"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
