        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-7016400"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p><a href="https://nebius.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7" class="user-hover" rel="712020:9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7" data-account-id="712020:9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7" accountid="712020:9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7" rel="noreferrer">Alexander Smirnov</a>  Thanks for the detailed feedback.</p>

<p>I have clarified User/UI behavior in the scenarios description:</p>

<ol>
	<li><b>Functionality will add options, but not replace them</b>. I clarified that the existing links remain unchanged and new links are appended below them, not replacing anything.</li>
	<li><b>Updated the description of the vertical list of links and the several link icons.</b> The vertical list now clearly refers to the combined set of links (existing + new).
	<ul>
		<li>Updated the description and added screenshots for clarity.</li>
		<li>If too much screen space is used, the details block can be collapsed so the database list remains visible without scrolling.</li>
		<li>The UI requests Grafana on page load only once. If the request fails or times out, static links are shown and the page loads normally (fallback).</li>
	</ul>
	</li>
	<li><b>There’s no mention that the links do not just to dashboards.</b> I added info that dashboards open with auto-filled <tt>ds</tt>, <tt>workspace</tt>, and <tt>database</tt> parameters.</li>
</ol>

        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-7033586"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Комментарий по  
                                                    
                
        
            <a class="user-hover" rel="712020:9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7"
                id="word_commented_712020:9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7"
                href="https://nebius.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7">
                    Alexander Smirnov
                </a>

                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">10/ноя/25</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-7033586"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p>Please have further comments/questions.</p>

<ol>
	<li>Why do you say ‘tag-based links’ for configuration? Do you expect this config section to be used for anything but Grafana?</li>
	<li>If I get it right, there’s an intermediate state when the page displays the static links, but still waits for the response from Grafana. What is shown at this moment?</li>
	<li>Dynamic refresh in background which moves other components is questionable in terms of UX, as the user can decide to click below, and right at this moment the contents are moved, so he clicks on the wrong place.</li>
	<li>There’s no need to request the list of dashboards from Grafana until the moment when the user decides to navigate to them.</li>
</ol>

        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-7036157"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Комментарий по  
                                                    
                
        
            <a class="user-hover" rel="712020:8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f"
                id="word_commented_712020:8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f"
                href="https://nebius.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f">
                    Andrei Rykov
                </a>

                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">11/ноя/25</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-7036157"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p><a href="https://nebius.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7" class="user-hover" rel="712020:9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7" data-account-id="712020:9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7" accountid="712020:9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7" rel="noreferrer">Alexander Smirnov</a> </p>

<blockquote><p>Why do you say ‘tag-based links’ for configuration?</p></blockquote>

<p>These are links that the UI loads using the Grafana API. The UI uses a known Grafana tag to perform the request.</p>

<blockquote><p>Do you expect this config section to be used for anything but Grafana?</p></blockquote>

<p>This section can be used for other links as well. I expect we will use this functionality.</p>

<blockquote><p>If I get it right, there’s an intermediate state when the page displays the static links, but still waits for the response from Grafana. What is shown at this moment?</p></blockquote>

<p>Not exactly. Grafana request happens before the page is rendered, asynchronously together with other requests to YDB. There should be a reasonable timeout for loading this data (1 sec). I think this request should be cached by tag, since the response is mostly the same and we have a single endpoint. There is no point to call the API repeatedly.</p>

<p>Depending on the result, there are two cases:</p>

<ol>
	<li>Successful load. All links are shown: static and those loaded by tag from Grafana.</li>
	<li>Failed load. Only static links are shown. А placeholder can be shown instead of the loaded dashboards (Failed to load dashboards)</li>
</ol>


<blockquote><p>Dynamic refresh in background which moves other components is questionable in terms of UX, as the user can decide to click below, and right at this moment the contents are moved, so he clicks on the wrong place.</p></blockquote>

<p>I would like to avoid this. I think a good solution is to make the Grafana request before rendering the page, as described above.</p>

<blockquote><p>There’s no need to request the list of dashboards from Grafana until the moment when the user decides to navigate to them.</p></blockquote>

<p>Preloading before the page is shown:</p>

<ul>
	<li>repeats the mechanism already used now for displaying YDB information</li>
	<li>will not take much time</li>
	<li>will allow showing the correct links immediately (no component movement)</li>
	<li>will usually be cached, so there is no reason not to use it</li>
</ul>

        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-7036202"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Комментарий по  
                                                    
                
        
            <a class="user-hover" rel="712020:9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7"
                id="word_commented_712020:9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7"
