        <tr id="comment-body-7036202"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p><a href="https://nebius.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f" class="user-hover" rel="712020:8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f" data-account-id="712020:8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f" accountid="712020:8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f" rel="noreferrer">Andrei Rykov</a> </p>

<p>If “these are links which use Grafana API” then why not to call it ‘Grafana links’? Also, we discussed earlier that we’re going to have a configuration section for Grafana integration, called ‘grafana:’ in the config yaml. Do you suggest to have anything alternate?</p>

<p>Re performing a request to Grafana before rendering the page, may I ask you to come up with other options? We can then compare them, and decide rationally why to choose which. Discussing only one option is not practical - there can be indefinite number of reasons both ‘for’ and ‘against’.</p>

<p>You told ‘grafana links’ are displayed. I would mention here that those links are already enriched with the ‘ds’ and ‘workspace’ parameters, to point to the dashboard for the current cluster,</p>
