        <tr id="comment-body-7036607"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p><a href="https://nebius.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7" class="user-hover" rel="712020:9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7" data-account-id="712020:9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7" accountid="712020:9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7" rel="noreferrer">Alexander Smirnov</a> </p>

<blockquote><p>If “these are links which use Grafana API” then why not to call it ‘Grafana links’? </p></blockquote>

<p>To avoid confusion, I needed to highlight that these Grafana links are loaded by tag. I expect there may also be links related to logs, for example. This is also Grafana, but they are not loaded by tag.</p>

<blockquote><p>Also, we discussed earlier that we’re going to have a configuration section for Grafana integration, called ‘grafana:’ in the config yaml. Do you suggest to have anything alternate?</p></blockquote>

<p>We’re going to have a configuration section for Grafan intergration. Not sure I understood the question. What does “alternate” mean?</p>

<p>We need to support links to non-Grafana resources too, for example, for diagnostics or documentation. I think the Grafana block should handle other sources as well. As far as I remember, we discussed this. You are okay with it, right?</p>

<blockquote><p>Re performing a request to Grafana before rendering the page, may I ask you to come up with other options? We can then compare them, and decide rationally why to choose which. Discussing only one option is not practical - there can be indefinite number of reasons both ‘for’ and ‘against’.</p></blockquote>

<p>I will write it in the next comment a bit later.</p>

<blockquote><p>You told ‘grafana links’ are displayed. I would mention here that those links are already enriched with the ‘ds’ and ‘workspace’ parameters, to point to the dashboard for the current cluster,</p></blockquote>

<p>One of the steps in the scenario: <tt>a new tab opens in Grafana with auto-filled parameters (ds, workspace)</tt></p>
