        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-7039189"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p><a href="https://nebius.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7" class="user-hover" rel="712020:9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7" data-account-id="712020:9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7" accountid="712020:9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7" rel="noreferrer">Alexander Smirnov</a> </p>

<blockquote><p>I would suggest rephrasing ‘If tag-based links are configured…’ to ‘If <b>Grafana</b> tag-based links are configured…’ to avoid both confusions.</p></blockquote>

<p>Agreed, this will be the best way.</p>

<blockquote><p>Other sources without Grafana specifics, just static links – yes, it must remain, yet we decided not to improve it anyhow as part of this ticket, just leave 3 existing options.</p></blockquote>

<p>Oh, now it's clear. It seems I missed the point that we decided not to improve other non-Grafana sources. I had the impression that the Grafana block should allow links to other sources, and I didn’t capture that correctly 😕 </p>

<blockquote><p>Yes I saw it, and this last step is ok. But I’m suggesting to add information about forging links to the step when they are loaded/displayed, to reveal the technological magic behind the last step.</p></blockquote>

<p>I will change it.</p>
        </td></tr>
