            [
                <font color="#336699">13/ноя/25</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-7047041"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p><a href="https://nebius.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f" class="user-hover" rel="712020:8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f" data-account-id="712020:8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f" accountid="712020:8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f" rel="noreferrer">Andrei Rykov</a> Grafana performs a request to get the list of dashboards <ins>at the moment</ins> when you <ins>click</ins> on the ‘Other dashboards’.</p>
        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-7048853"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Комментарий по  
                                                    
                
        
            <a class="user-hover" rel="712020:8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f"
                id="word_commented_712020:8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f"
                href="https://nebius.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f">
                    Andrei Rykov
                </a>

                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">13/ноя/25</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-7048853"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p><a href="https://nebius.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7" class="user-hover" rel="712020:9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7" data-account-id="712020:9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7" accountid="712020:9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7" rel="noreferrer">Alexander Smirnov</a> </p>

<blockquote><p>Grafana performs a request to get the list of dashboards <ins>at the moment</ins> when you <ins>click</ins> on the ‘Other dashboards’.</p></blockquote>

<p>Below I listed the possible options for how to perform requests to Grafana.</p>

<ol>
	<li><b>Request handled by meta</b></li>
</ol>


<p>+ Simpler frontend implementation.<br/>
– Meta needs access to Grafana.<br/>
– If Grafana is unavailable, meta responses will be delayed.</p>

<ol>
	<li><b>Request on page load - waiting for Grafana response</b></li>
</ol>


<p>+ Simpler and more predictable frontend implementation.<br/>
– If Grafana responds slowly, the page load will be delayed.</p>

<ol>
	<li><b>Request on page load - not waiting for Grafana response</b><br/>
<em>The UI shows a loading spinner or skeleton on page while waiting for the response.</em></li>
</ol>


<p>+ Fast page load.<br/>
– Higher frontend complexity to display data smoothly.</p>

<ol>
	<li><b>Request on button click, with a short timeout (Grafana-style variant)</b><br/>
<em>The UI quickly renders a pop-up with the dashboard list or an error message.</em></li>
</ol>


<p>+ Fast page load.<br/>
+ No requests if the user doesn’t need the data.<br/>
+ Always up-to-date information.<br/>
– If Grafana responds slowly, the user won’t see the dashboard list (cache reduces this issue)</p>

<ol>
	<li><b>Request on button click, with a long timeout (as implemented in Grafana)</b><br/>
<em>The UI shows a loading spinner or skeleton in pop-up while waiting for the response.</em></li>
</ol>


<p>+ Fast page load.<br/>
+ No requests if the user doesn’t need the data.<br/>
+ Always up-to-date information.<br/>
– Higher frontend complexity to display data smoothly.</p>

<p>For myself, I decided that options 2 and 4 are better because they are simple and predictable.</p>
        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-7059196"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Комментарий по  
                                                    
                
        
            <a class="user-hover" rel="712020:9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7"
                id="word_commented_712020:9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7"
                href="https://nebius.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7">
                    Alexander Smirnov
                </a>

                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">17/ноя/25</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-7059196"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p><a href="https://nebius.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f" class="user-hover" rel="712020:8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f" data-account-id="712020:8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f" accountid="712020:8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f" rel="noreferrer">Andrei Rykov</a> Ok, now when we have all options, let me add some pros/cons against your preferable options (2/4) and mine (5). Great that you have added the one about ‘Always up-to-date information’ by yourself – it was one of those I was going to add as a ‘pro’ for 4 and 5. Also, it’s better to ensure that some feature which is listed among ‘pros’ somewhere is also list among ‘cons’ in other places.</p>

<p>2:</p>

<ul class="alternate" type="square">
	<li>More requests to Grafana than needed (reverse to “No requests if the user doesn’t need the data”). I would estimate about 100x more requests (out of 100 page shows there will be only 1 when the user really wants to go to a Grafana dashboard then)</li>
</ul>


<ul class="alternate" type="square">
	<li>Page needs to be fully reloaded to see the fresh list (reverse to “Always up-to-date information“). Usually makes no difference, but can be noticeable when the user changes the list on Grafana side, and also can lead to wasting time with public users when we fix something in Grafana in this list.</li>
</ul>


<ul class="alternate" type="square">
	<li>Different behaviour between navigation <span class="error">&#91;YDB UI &gt; Grafana&#93;</span> and <span class="error">&#91;Grafana &gt; Grafana&#93;</span>.</li>
</ul>


<p>4:</p>

<ul class="alternate" type="square">
	<li>Nervous behaviour for user comparing to option 5. He clicked, nothing has shown. He clicks again, and again. It pops up but he already clicked another time, and nothing again. Using cached information changes the option, as we lose the ‘Always up-to-date information' feature.</li>
</ul>


<p>+ Consistent behaviour between navigation <span class="error">&#91;YDB UI &gt; Grafana&#93;</span> and <span class="error">&#91;Grafana &gt; Grafana&#93;</span> (when Grafana responds fast)</p>

<p>5:</p>

<p>+ Clear behaviour for user comparing to option 4. He clicked, saw the spinner, waits until the contents show.</p>

<p>+ Consistent behaviour between navigation <span class="error">&#91;YDB UI &gt; Grafana&#93;</span> and <span class="error">&#91;Grafana &gt; Grafana&#93;</span> even if Grafana responds slow</p>



<p>Concluding, looks like the only remaining minus of the option 5 is the complexity on the UI side. Have you asked them if it’s really difficult to implement? Also, the UI solution here can be used for other dynamic links to other systems we can integrate with in the future, not only for Grafana.</p>
        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-7065952"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Комментарий по  
                                                    
                
        
            <a class="user-hover" rel="712020:8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f"
                id="word_commented_712020:8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f"
                href="https://nebius.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f">
                    Andrei Rykov
                </a>

                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">18/ноя/25</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-7065952"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p><a href="https://nebius.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7" class="user-hover" rel="712020:9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7" data-account-id="712020:9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7" accountid="712020:9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7" rel="noreferrer">Alexander Smirnov</a> Thanks for the detailed feedback.</p>

<p>Unfortunately, one important thing I missed: fetching the dashboard list from Grafana in the UI requires a cross-domain request. Browsers block such requests unless CORS is configured on the Grafana side. Setting up CORS for Grafana in our environment is quite complex, and without a strong business justification it is unlikely to be prioritized.</p>

<p>With this limitation, I’m afraid, the only realistic option that remains is <b>Option 1: Request handled by meta</b>, since meta can access Grafana without browser restrictions.</p>

<p>Moreover, I found another limitation of the <b>Option 1</b> solution that affects usability: the list of dashboards for test clusters must be provided through <a href="https://grafana.testing.nebius.dev/" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://grafana.testing.nebius.dev/</a> rather than <a href="https://grafana.nebius.dev/" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://grafana.nebius.dev/</a> as usual. This happens because one site is in the production environment and the other is in the test environment. I plan to clarify whether the information is synchronized between them in any form and what the possible solution options for the test clusters might look like.</p>
        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-7069792"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Комментарий по  
                                                    
                
        
            <a class="user-hover" rel="712020:8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f"
                id="word_commented_712020:8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f"
                href="https://nebius.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A8b69336d-51ba-4e44-920f-ddf22872c09f">
                    Andrei Rykov
                </a>

                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">19/ноя/25</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-7069792"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p><a href="https://nebius.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7" class="user-hover" rel="712020:9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7" data-account-id="712020:9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7" accountid="712020:9b6f6940-7c5c-486d-b283-abfb0ef8b2e7" rel="noreferrer">Alexander Smirnov</a> To continue, I’ve gathered enough information to reason about the available options.<br/>
It is definitely possible to teach Meta to access Grafana and fetch the list of dashboards - all the necessary pieces are available:</p>

<ul>
	<li>Meta can be given network access to Grafana.</li>
	<li>It’s enough to perform an HTTP request using the Grafana service account token provided by the Grafana duty team</li>
</ul>


<p>Example:</p>

<div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"><div class="preformattedContent panelContent">
<pre>curl -i 'https://grafana.nebius.dev/api/search?tag=ydb-common' \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer {token}" \
  -H "Accept: application/json"</pre>
</div></div>

<p>As we discussed verbally, it’s not necessary for Meta to access Grafana during the cluster request - it can be a separate request. This gets rid of Meta’s dependency on Grafana for responses. In that sense, we could say that options 2–5 are still valid if we replace the Grafana request with a Meta request.</p>

<p>I also reviewed how the dropdown behaves in Grafana, which gives us new option:</p>

<p><b>Option 6: Request to Meta on button click, with a long timeout (as implemented in Grafana)</b><br/>
<em>The UI shows a pop-up only when the response is received. If Grafana is unavailable, the pop-up does not appear.</em></p>

<p>+ Fast page load.<br/>
+ No requests if the user doesn’t need the data.<br/>
+ Always up-to-date information.<br/>
+ Simpler frontend implementation.<br/>
+ No different behaviour between navigation in YDB UI and Grafana<br/>
– Meta needs access to Grafana.<br/>
– If Grafana responds slowly, user don’t see UI reaction after click<br/>
– No static links in pop-up (fewer options for the pop-up design)</p>
        </td></tr>
            </table>
